        <body>
            <div type="edition" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="grc" resp="#VM">
                <ab>
                    <lb n="1"/><orig>Π</orig>
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus">
                <listApp>
                    <app loc="1"><note>Text after Guzzardi 2012, 174 n. 61.</note></app>
                </listApp>
            </div>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#VM">
                <p>Pi-shaped mark.</p>
            </div>
            <div type="commentary">
                <p>Guzzardi records this sign, resembling Greek pi, on one of two further blocks in the same masonry structure within 
                    the perimeter of the cella as the block bearing the sigma-shaped mark. The publication supplies neither an illustration 
                    nor measurements of the individual block. Its context places it within the same construction phase, dated to the late sixth 
                    or early fifth century BCE. Comparable signs on blocks from the temple are interpreted as setting-out marks used to guide 
                    their positioning and orientation.</p>
            </div>
